You receive some messages from them {"6": [{"message_id": 2, "content": "Hello everyone! I'm here to discuss the 1965 Mustang Fastback. I'm very interested in its objective value and would like to explore how we can best determine a fair price. My initial assessment suggests a value significantly influenced by its rarity and condition. I'm proposing we establish a baseline for negotiation based on verifiable data. What are your thoughts on approaching this logically to ensure a mutually beneficial outcome?", "sender_id": 10, "sent_at": "2026-03-29 07:19:36.093376"}, {"message_id": 7, "content": "That's an excellent starting point. I agree that focusing on objective value is key. To that end, I suggest we compile data on recent sales of comparable 1965 Mustang Fastbacks, factoring in condition, mileage, and any unique historical significance. We can also research current market trends and expert assessments. Would you be open to sharing any documentation or assessments you have regarding the car's condition and history? This will help us establish a robust baseline for our discussion.", "sender_id": 10, "sent_at": "2026-03-29 07:24:48.410656"}, {"message_id": 8, "content": "Silas, I appreciate your logical approach to determining the Mustang's value. I agree that verifiable data is key. Regarding a baseline, considering the car's rarity and condition, I've seen comparable models recently auctioning for approximately 20% below the initial estimates due to market fluctuations. Perhaps we could use a figure around that benchmark as a starting point for our negotiation? I'm eager to hear your thoughts on this.", "sender_id": 11, "sent_at": "2026-03-29 07:25:18.103396"}, {"message_id": 16, "content": "Silas, I understand your desire to compile comprehensive data, and I'm certainly open to reviewing any documentation you have on the Mustang's history and condition. To give you a clearer picture of my position, based on my research into recent sales of similar vehicles and current market trends, I'd be prepared to offer around $100,000. This figure reflects a discount that I believe accounts for current market conditions and potential restoration needs. I'm keen to see what documentation you have to further inform our discussion.", "sender_id": 11, "sent_at": "2026-03-29 07:36:04.429576"}, {"message_id": 17, "content": "I understand your perspective on using a figure around 20% below the initial estimates as a starting point, and I appreciate you sharing that. My aim is to establish a robust, data-driven valuation for the Mustang. To that end, I'm keen to explore recent comparable sales data. Do you have specific auction results or market analyses that support the '20% below estimate' benchmark, or perhaps indicate a price point closer to your target of 10% above the estimate? Understanding the objective benchmarks that inform these figures will be crucial for us to find a mutually agreeable price.", "sender_id": 10, "sent_at": "2026-03-29 07:36:55.621936"}]}
